{"aki":{"flowcharts":[],"valueTables":[{"id":"arf-prerenal-vs-atn","title":"Urine and blood indices separating prerenal azotaemia from oliguric acute tubular necrosis","columns":["Parameter","Prerenal azotemia","Oliguric ARF (ATN)"],"rows":[{"parameter":"BUN/creatinine ratio (BUN, not urea)","unit":"ratio","cells":[{"text":"{{hy:>20:1}}","op":">","value":20},{"text":"10-15:1","range":[10,15]}],"cite":"c2"},{"parameter":"Urine sodium (UNa)","unit":"mEq/L","cells":[{"text":"<20","op":"<","value":20},{"text":">40","op":">","value":40}],"cite":"c2"},{"parameter":"Urine osmolality","unit":"mOsm/kg H2O","cells":[{"text":">500","op":">","value":500},{"text":"<350","op":"<","value":350}],"cite":"c2"},{"parameter":"Fractional excretion of sodium (FENa)","unit":"%","cells":[{"text":"{{hy:<1%}}","op":"<","value":1},{"text":"{{hy:>2%}}","op":">","value":2}],"cite":"c2"},{"parameter":"Urine/plasma creatinine ratio","unit":"ratio","cells":[{"text":">40","op":">","value":40},{"text":"<20","op":"<","value":20}],"cite":"c2"},{"parameter":"Urinary casts","cells":[{"text":"None, or hyaline/granular"},{"text":"Muddy brown"}],"cite":"c2"}],"footnote":"FENa (%) = (UNa x PCr x 100) / (PNa x UCr), where U = urine and P = plasma. FENa is unreliable after diuretics, in sepsis, with contrast-associated AKI and in CKD; interpret with the clinical picture."}],"citations":[{"id":"c2","label":"Table 61-2, user-supplied; source edition not shown (laboratory findings in acute renal failure)","kind":"user-supplied"}],"status":"ai_drafted"}}